{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SeAVh6SvjL2qE7v1prSavG","type":"tool_result","content":"=== EVIDENCE ===\n{\"claim\":\"external\",\"confidence\":1.0,\"id\":\"E-BLUEPRINT\",\"source\":{\"captured_at\":\"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\",\"sha256\":\"f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\",\"uri\":\"tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\"},\"summary\":\"Synthetic blueprint fixture describing the rate-limiting steel thread.\"}\n=== TELEMETRY ===\n{\"attributes\":{\"source\":{\"name\":\"source-recipe.yaml\",\"sha256\":\"c9aa28e2046f2bde0bdc707800caccd9640f837f25505b75f41d09adec2afa0b\"}},\"authorization\":false,\"event\":\"taskspec.decompose.map\",\"schema_version\":1,\"time\":\"2026-09-14T21:29:49.200765+00:00\",\"token\":\"SEAM_MAP=READY\"}\n{\"attributes\":{\"lanes\":4,\"legs\":4},\"authorization\":false,\"event\":\"taskspec.decompose.plan\",\"schema_version\":1,\"time\":\"2026-09-14T21:29:49.284082+00:00\",\"token\":\"DELIVERY_PLAN=NEEDS_REVIEW\"}\n=== PROPOSED-GRAPH ===\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"TASK_GRAPH=READY\",\n  \"plan_sha256\": \"09cb242fff217acfd43a52388bcf67c42596a99d2c4c14202156b47009863a03\",\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"title\": \"Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/decision.py\",\n        \"tests/test_decision_visibility.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"title\": \"Resolve one effective organization policy\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.py\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_resolution.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"title\": \"Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_schema.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"title\": \"Enforce the effective limit at request 101\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\",\n        \"tests/test_request_101.py\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contentions\": [],\n  \"critical_path\": [\n    \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n    \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n    \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n    \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\"\n  ],\n  \"critical_path_mermaid_sha256\": \"5ca6564fc3a4130a4f4de657714b91b354f60038f0d2902e908e1c7bad005824\"\n}\n=== SOURCE-RECIPE ===\nschema_version: 1\nintent:\n  id: DI-RATE-LIMIT\n  title: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n  summary: >-\n    For every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy,\n    deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason\n    plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n    - Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Policy contract boundary\n    - Effective policy resolver\n    - Request enforcement boundary\n    - Decision response and telemetry boundary\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Organization identity supplied by the host application\n    - Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\n  unknowns: []\nevidence:\n  - id: E-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: external\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1.0\n    summary: Synthetic blueprint fixture describing the rate-limiting steel thread.\ndecisions:\n  - id: ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\n    status: accepted\n    owner: example-fixture\n    rationale: >-\n      The fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy,\n      request 101 enforcement, then visible reason and decision telemetry.\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\n    name: Policy contract\n    description: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\n    consumes: [authored organization policy]\n    produces: [validated policy document]\n    owner: platform-contracts\n    independent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n        reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n      name: Policy contract lane\n      owner: platform-contracts\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n          observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n          proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n          requires: []\n          produces: [validated policy document]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n              title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n              goal: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\n              done_condition: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n                - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: a policy with a positive limit and window\n                  when: the document is validated\n                  then: schema validation succeeds\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: a policy with a zero limit or window\n                  when: the document is validated\n                  then: schema validation fails\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The policy schema exists and parses as JSON\n                  bash: test -f src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json && python3 -m json.tool src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json >/dev/null\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Valid policy examples pass the schema tests\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k valid\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Invalid non-positive values are rejected\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: encode limits only in handler constants\n                  reason: downstream resolution would have no versioned contract\n                  instead: validate one explicit schema before resolution\n                - action: accept zero or negative windows\n                  reason: enforcement semantics would be undefined\n                  instead: reject non-positive values at the contract boundary\n                - action: couple the schema to one storage provider\n                  reason: policy shape and persistence are separate decisions\n                  instead: keep the schema provider-neutral\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\n              observability: policy schema test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: Separates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Resolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\n    consumes: [validated policy document, organization identity]\n    produces: [effective policy decision]\n    owner: policy-runtime\n    independent_proof: A deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter\n        reason: Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n      name: Effective policy lane\n      owner: policy-runtime\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n          observable_state: Every organization has one effective policy decision\n          proof: Defaults and organization overrides resolve with deterministic precedence.\n          requires: [validated policy document]\n          produces: [effective policy decision]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-effective-policy\n              title: Resolve one effective organization policy\n              goal: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\n              done_condition: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-policy-schema]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/policy.py\n                - tests/test_policy_resolution.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: a valid organization override\n                  when: effective policy is resolved\n                  then: the override and its provenance are returned\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: no organization override\n                  when: effective policy is resolved\n                  then: the validated default and its provenance are returned\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Organization overrides win deterministically\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k override\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Defaults resolve when no override exists\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k default\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Resolution returns policy provenance\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k provenance\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: hide precedence inside conditional request code\n                  reason: effective policy would not be independently testable\n                  instead: expose one deterministic resolver\n                - action: return a policy without provenance\n                  reason: operators could not explain the enforcement decision\n                  instead: return source and version with the policy\n                - action: silently invent a default\n                  reason: missing policy is an ownership decision\n                  instead: require a validated explicit default\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\n              observability: effective policy resolution test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n    name: Request enforcement\n    description: Separates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Apply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n    consumes: [effective policy decision, organization identity, current request count]\n    produces: [allow-or-deny decision]\n    owner: request-runtime\n    independent_proof: A boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Infer enforcement from emitted metrics\n        reason: Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n      name: Request enforcement lane\n      owner: request-runtime\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n          observable_state: Request 101 is denied for a limit of 100\n          proof: Boundary tests allow the first 100 requests and deny the next request once.\n          requires: [effective policy decision]\n          produces: [allow-or-deny decision]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-request-101\n              title: Enforce the effective limit at request 101\n              goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n              done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-effective-policy]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n                - tests/test_request_101.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n                  when: request 100 is evaluated\n                  then: the request is allowed\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n                  when: request 101 is evaluated\n                  then: the request is denied exactly once\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Request 100 remains allowed\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Request 101 is denied\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n                  reason: request 101 would pass through\n                  instead: decide before forwarding work\n                - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n                  reason: observation is not authorization\n                  instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n                - action: share counters across organizations\n                  reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n                  instead: key state by organization and window\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n              observability: boundary test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n    name: Decision visibility\n    description: Separates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Present a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n    consumes: [allow-or-deny decision]\n    produces: [visible reason, decision telemetry event]\n    owner: reliability-interface\n    independent_proof: Response and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Emit a metric without returning a stable reason\n        reason: Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n      name: Decision visibility lane\n      owner: reliability-interface\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\n          observable_state: Denials expose a stable reason and matching decision telemetry\n          proof: The response reason and telemetry payload share one decision identifier.\n          requires: [allow-or-deny decision]\n          produces: [visible reason, decision telemetry event]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-decision-visibility\n              title: Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\n              goal: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\n              done_condition: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-request-101]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/decision.py\n                - tests/test_decision_visibility.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: request 101 is denied\n                  when: the response is created\n                  then: it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: the same denial decision\n                  when: telemetry is emitted\n                  then: it carries the same reason and decision identifier\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The response exposes the stable denial reason\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k response_reason\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Telemetry carries the matching reason\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k telemetry_reason\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Response and telemetry share a decision identifier\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k decision_identifier\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: expose an unstable free-text reason\n                  reason: clients and operators could not depend on it\n                  instead: use a stable machine reason plus human detail\n                - action: let telemetry authorize the denial\n                  reason: observation cannot cross the enforcement boundary\n                  instead: emit only after receiving the decision\n                - action: omit decision lineage\n                  reason: response and telemetry could not be correlated\n                  instead: carry one decision identifier across both outputs\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n              observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\nsteel_thread:\n  - LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n  - LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n  - LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n  - LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION\n    status: FIXED\n    summary: Metering was removed from the canonical steel thread and kept external.\n    owner: example-fixture\n    rationale: The accepted boundary decision leaves metering outside the four-leg proving path.\ncontentions: []","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6624e82c-6454-45a5-b85d-1c433f495bcc","uuid":"2129346a-7619-44c5-9cf2-cf682c01251f","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:30:13.634Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== EVIDENCE ===\n{\"claim\":\"external\",\"confidence\":1.0,\"id\":\"E-BLUEPRINT\",\"source\":{\"captured_at\":\"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\",\"sha256\":\"f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\",\"uri\":\"tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\"},\"summary\":\"Synthetic blueprint fixture describing the rate-limiting steel thread.\"}\n=== TELEMETRY ===\n{\"attributes\":{\"source\":{\"name\":\"source-recipe.yaml\",\"sha256\":\"c9aa28e2046f2bde0bdc707800caccd9640f837f25505b75f41d09adec2afa0b\"}},\"authorization\":false,\"event\":\"taskspec.decompose.map\",\"schema_version\":1,\"time\":\"2026-09-14T21:29:49.200765+00:00\",\"token\":\"SEAM_MAP=READY\"}\n{\"attributes\":{\"lanes\":4,\"legs\":4},\"authorization\":false,\"event\":\"taskspec.decompose.plan\",\"schema_version\":1,\"time\":\"2026-09-14T21:29:49.284082+00:00\",\"token\":\"DELIVERY_PLAN=NEEDS_REVIEW\"}\n=== PROPOSED-GRAPH ===\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"TASK_GRAPH=READY\",\n  \"plan_sha256\": \"09cb242fff217acfd43a52388bcf67c42596a99d2c4c14202156b47009863a03\",\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"title\": \"Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/decision.py\",\n        \"tests/test_decision_visibility.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"title\": \"Resolve one effective organization policy\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.py\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_resolution.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"title\": \"Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_schema.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"title\": \"Enforce the effective limit at request 101\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\",\n        \"tests/test_request_101.py\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contentions\": [],\n  \"critical_path\": [\n    \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n    \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n    \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n    \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\"\n  ],\n  \"critical_path_mermaid_sha256\": \"5ca6564fc3a4130a4f4de657714b91b354f60038f0d2902e908e1c7bad005824\"\n}\n=== SOURCE-RECIPE ===\nschema_version: 1\nintent:\n  id: DI-RATE-LIMIT\n  title: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n  summary: >-\n    For every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy,\n    deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason\n    plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n    - Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Policy contract boundary\n    - Effective policy resolver\n    - Request enforcement boundary\n    - Decision response and telemetry boundary\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Organization identity supplied by the host application\n    - Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\n  unknowns: []\nevidence:\n  - id: E-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: external\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1.0\n    summary: Synthetic blueprint fixture describing the rate-limiting steel thread.\ndecisions:\n  - id: ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\n    status: accepted\n    owner: example-fixture\n    rationale: >-\n      The fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy,\n      request 101 enforcement, then visible reason and decision telemetry.\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\n    name: Policy contract\n    description: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\n    consumes: [authored organization policy]\n    produces: [validated policy document]\n    owner: platform-contracts\n    independent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n        reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n      name: Policy contract lane\n      owner: platform-contracts\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n          observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n          proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n          requires: []\n          produces: [validated policy document]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n              title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n              goal: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\n              done_condition: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n                - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: a policy with a positive limit and window\n                  when: the document is validated\n                  then: schema validation succeeds\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: a policy with a zero limit or window\n                  when: the document is validated\n                  then: schema validation fails\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The policy schema exists and parses as JSON\n                  bash: test -f src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json && python3 -m json.tool src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json >/dev/null\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Valid policy examples pass the schema tests\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k valid\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Invalid non-positive values are rejected\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: encode limits only in handler constants\n                  reason: downstream resolution would have no versioned contract\n                  instead: validate one explicit schema before resolution\n                - action: accept zero or negative windows\n                  reason: enforcement semantics would be undefined\n                  instead: reject non-positive values at the contract boundary\n                - action: couple the schema to one storage provider\n                  reason: policy shape and persistence are separate decisions\n                  instead: keep the schema provider-neutral\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\n              observability: policy schema test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: Separates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Resolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\n    consumes: [validated policy document, organization identity]\n    produces: [effective policy decision]\n    owner: policy-runtime\n    independent_proof: A deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter\n        reason: Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n      name: Effective policy lane\n      owner: policy-runtime\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n          observable_state: Every organization has one effective policy decision\n          proof: Defaults and organization overrides resolve with deterministic precedence.\n          requires: [validated policy document]\n          produces: [effective policy decision]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-effective-policy\n              title: Resolve one effective organization policy\n              goal: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\n              done_condition: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-policy-schema]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/policy.py\n                - tests/test_policy_resolution.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: a valid organization override\n                  when: effective policy is resolved\n                  then: the override and its provenance are returned\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: no organization override\n                  when: effective policy is resolved\n                  then: the validated default and its provenance are returned\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Organization overrides win deterministically\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k override\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Defaults resolve when no override exists\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k default\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Resolution returns policy provenance\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k provenance\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: hide precedence inside conditional request code\n                  reason: effective policy would not be independently testable\n                  instead: expose one deterministic resolver\n                - action: return a policy without provenance\n                  reason: operators could not explain the enforcement decision\n                  instead: return source and version with the policy\n                - action: silently invent a default\n                  reason: missing policy is an ownership decision\n                  instead: require a validated explicit default\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\n              observability: effective policy resolution test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n    name: Request enforcement\n    description: Separates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Apply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n    consumes: [effective policy decision, organization identity, current request count]\n    produces: [allow-or-deny decision]\n    owner: request-runtime\n    independent_proof: A boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Infer enforcement from emitted metrics\n        reason: Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n      name: Request enforcement lane\n      owner: request-runtime\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n          observable_state: Request 101 is denied for a limit of 100\n          proof: Boundary tests allow the first 100 requests and deny the next request once.\n          requires: [effective policy decision]\n          produces: [allow-or-deny decision]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-request-101\n              title: Enforce the effective limit at request 101\n              goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n              done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-effective-policy]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n                - tests/test_request_101.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n                  when: request 100 is evaluated\n                  then: the request is allowed\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n                  when: request 101 is evaluated\n                  then: the request is denied exactly once\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Request 100 remains allowed\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Request 101 is denied\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n                  reason: request 101 would pass through\n                  instead: decide before forwarding work\n                - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n                  reason: observation is not authorization\n                  instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n                - action: share counters across organizations\n                  reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n                  instead: key state by organization and window\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n              observability: boundary test pass count\n  - id: SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n    name: Decision visibility\n    description: Separates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n    evidence: [E-BLUEPRINT]\n    responsibility: Present a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n    consumes: [allow-or-deny decision]\n    produces: [visible reason, decision telemetry event]\n    owner: reliability-interface\n    independent_proof: Response and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n    decision_ids: [ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER]\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Emit a metric without returning a stable reason\n        reason: Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n      name: Decision visibility lane\n      owner: reliability-interface\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\n          observable_state: Denials expose a stable reason and matching decision telemetry\n          proof: The response reason and telemetry payload share one decision identifier.\n          requires: [allow-or-deny decision]\n          produces: [visible reason, decision telemetry event]\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20260802-decision-visibility\n              title: Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\n              goal: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\n              done_condition: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: any\n              required_tools: [git, bash, python3, pytest]\n              depends_on: [T-20260802-request-101]\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/rate_limit/decision.py\n                - tests/test_decision_visibility.py\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: request 101 is denied\n                  when: the response is created\n                  then: it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: the same denial decision\n                  when: telemetry is emitted\n                  then: it carries the same reason and decision identifier\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: The response exposes the stable denial reason\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k response_reason\n                  verifies: [B-1]\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Telemetry carries the matching reason\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k telemetry_reason\n                  verifies: [B-2]\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Response and telemetry share a decision identifier\n                  bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k decision_identifier\n                  verifies: [B-1, B-2]\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: expose an unstable free-text reason\n                  reason: clients and operators could not depend on it\n                  instead: use a stable machine reason plus human detail\n                - action: let telemetry authorize the denial\n                  reason: observation cannot cross the enforcement boundary\n                  instead: emit only after receiving the decision\n                - action: omit decision lineage\n                  reason: response and telemetry could not be correlated\n                  instead: carry one decision identifier across both outputs\n              do_not_touch: [tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md]\n              rollback: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n              observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\nsteel_thread:\n  - LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n  - LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n  - LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n  - LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION\n    status: FIXED\n    summary: Metering was removed from the canonical steel thread and kept external.\n    owner: example-fixture\n    rationale: The accepted boundary decision leaves metering outside the four-leg proving path.\ncontentions: []","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
