{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJWzhJmC1VHDvDnBtZazg4","type":"tool_result","content":"# Task-Spec repository configuration (no credentials)\nbacklog_dir=tasks\nresearch_provider=none\n=== AUTHORED head ===\nschema_version: 1\nintent:\n  id: DI-RATE-LIMIT\n  title: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n  summary: >-\n    For every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy,\n    deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason\n    plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n    - Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Policy contract boundary\n    - Effective policy resolver\n    - Request enforcement boundary\n    - Decision response and telemetry boundary\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Organization identity supplied by the host application\n    - Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\n  unknowns: []\nevidence:\n  - id: E-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: external\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1.0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6624e82c-6454-45a5-b85d-1c433f495bcc","uuid":"3607cedd-7cc0-47af-8f5e-7d2591e5b61f","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:30:32.280Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Task-Spec repository configuration (no credentials)\nbacklog_dir=tasks\nresearch_provider=none\n=== AUTHORED head ===\nschema_version: 1\nintent:\n  id: DI-RATE-LIMIT\n  title: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n  summary: >-\n    For every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy,\n    deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason\n    plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n    - Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\nsystem_map:\n  claim: proposed\n  components:\n    - Policy contract boundary\n    - Effective policy resolver\n    - Request enforcement boundary\n    - Decision response and telemetry boundary\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Organization identity supplied by the host application\n    - Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\n  unknowns: []\nevidence:\n  - id: E-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: external\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-08-02T00:00:00Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1.0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
