{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf43aqLPmmvgABRzei6xo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I inspected the recorded artifacts and the CLI state. Almost everything is already settled — only one thing is genuinely open.\n\n## What's already recorded (no decision needed)\n\n| Artifact | State |\n|---|---|\n| `intent.md` (DI-RATE-LIMIT) | proposed, 4 success criteria, 2 out-of-scope items |\n| `system-map.md` | `unknowns: []` — nothing left open |\n| `ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER` | **accepted** (schema → effective policy → request 101 → visible reason) |\n| `OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION` | **FIXED** — metering kept external to the steel thread |\n| `seam-map.yaml` | `SEAM_MAP=READY`, 4 seams with owners |\n| `delivery-plan.yaml` | 4 lanes, 4 legs, `contentions: []` |\n| `proposed-graph.json` | `TASK_GRAPH=READY`, 4 tasks, linear critical path |\n| `authored.yaml` vs `source-recipe.yaml` | byte-identical (`c9aa28e2…`) — prepare is done |\n\nThe two things that *look* like open questions aren't: the counter/window storage adapter is deliberately deferred (\"implementation-selected\"), and production storage/deployment is explicitly listed as out of scope in the intent.\n\n## The one missing decision\n\n**Your explicit acceptance of the delivery-plan topology.** `tasks/.plans/rate-limit/reviews/` is empty, and the engine blocks on exactly this:\n\n```\n$ taskspec decompose compile rate-limit\nDECOMPOSE=INVALID plan_not_ready: Delivery plan is not marked ready.;\n                  review_missing: An accepted delivery-plan review is required.\n```\n\nThe plan sits at `DELIVERY_PLAN=NEEDS_REVIEW`. Compile — and everything after it — is gated until a signed review exists. This is an authorization I can't supply for you; it has to carry a reviewer identity and a reason.\n\nSo, my question:\n\n> **Do you accept the four-lane / four-leg topology as recorded, and what reviewer name and reason should the review record carry?**\n\nIf yes, this is the command — confirm and I'll run it, or run it yourself:\n\n```\ntaskspec decompose review rate-limit --accept \\\n  --reviewer \"<your name>\" \\\n  --reason \"<why you accept this topology>\"\n```\n\nOne note: `taskspec decompose status rate-limit` prints `NEXT: taskspec decompose prepare … --recipe <file>`, but that hint is stale — the recipe is already prepared and hashes match the seam map. `review` is the real next step."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":30684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":542},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6624e82c-6454-45a5-b85d-1c433f495bcc","uuid":"97e7d74f-4b70-49e2-9263-cf1a7a7badbf","timestamp":"2026-09-14T21:31:16.764Z","request_id":"req_011Cf43apn9s7eNWyEpNPDnJ"}
